                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma, x:\mathbb{N} \vdash C(x):\mathrm{Type}_i \quad \Gamma \vdash c_0:C(0) \quad \Gamma \vdash c_s:\prod_{x:\mathbb{N}} C(x) \to C(s(x))}{\Gamma \vdash \mathrm{up}_\mathbb{N}^C(c_0, c_s):\exists!c:\prod_{x:\mathbb{N}} C(x).(c(0) =_{C(0)} c_0) \times \prod_{x:\mathbb{N}} c(s(x)) =_{C(s(x))} c_s(c(x))}
          %h3#with_a_separate_type_judgment_and_type_variables With a separate type judgment and type variables
          %p
            In this section, we describe a formalization of propositional type theory using a type judgment, in the style of
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Rijke22"} Rijke 2022
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory+with+type+variables"} type variables
          %h4#judgments_and_contexts Judgments and contexts
          %p This presentation of propositional type theory consists of the following judgments:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Type judgments, where we judge
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                to be a type,
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \; \mathrm{type}
            %li
              %p
                Element judgments, where we judge
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
                to be an element of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:A
            %li
              %p
                Context judgments, where we judge
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
                to be a context,
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Γ
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \; \mathrm{ctx}
          %p Contexts are lists of type judgments and element judgments, et cetera, and are formalized by the rules for the empty context and extending the context by a type judgment and by an element judgment
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                  %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                  %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{}{() \; \mathrm{ctx}} \qquad \frac{\Gamma \; \mathrm{ctx}}{(\Gamma, A \; \mathrm{type}) \; \mathrm{ctx}} \qquad \frac{\Gamma \; \mathrm{ctx} \quad \Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type}}{(\Gamma, a:A) \; \mathrm{ctx}}
          %h4#variable_rules Variable rules
          %p
            There are two additional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structural+rules"} structural rules
            in propositional type theory, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variable+rule"} variable rule
            for types and elements.
          %p The variable rule for types states that we may derive a type judgment if the type judgment is in the context already:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Δ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma, A \; \mathrm{type}, \Delta \; \mathrm{ctx}}{\Gamma, A \; \mathrm{type}, \Delta \vdash A \; \mathrm{type}}
          %p The variable rule for elements states that we may derive a element judgment if the element judgment is in the context already:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Δ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma, a:A, \Delta \; \mathrm{ctx}}{\Gamma, a:A, \Delta \vdash a:A}
          %h4#families_of_types_and_elements_2 Families of types and elements
          %p
            A family of types is a type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            in the context of the element judgment
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mi B
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A \vdash B \; \mathrm{type}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(x)
            to indicate its dependence upon
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(a)
            is a type dependent upon
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:A
          %p
            A family of elements is an element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b:B
            in the context of the variable judgment
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mi b
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A \vdash b:B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b(x)
            to indicate its dependence upon
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b(a)
            is an element dependent upon
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:A
          %p
            A universal family of types is a type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            in the context of a type variable judgment
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \; \mathrm{type}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mi B
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \; \mathrm{type} \vdash B \; \mathrm{type}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(X)
            to indicate its dependence upon
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \; \mathrm{type}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(A)
            is a type dependent upon
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            A universal family of elements is an element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b:B
            in the context of the type variable judgment
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \; \mathrm{type}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mi b
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \; \mathrm{type} \vdash b:B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b(X)
            to indicate its dependence upon
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \; \mathrm{type}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b(A)
            is an element dependent upon
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \; \mathrm{type}
          %h4#identity_types_2 Identity types
          %p Formation rules for identity types:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi a
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mi A
                      %mi b
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma, a:A, b:A \vdash a =_A b \; \mathrm{type}}
          %p Introduction rules for identity types:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} refl
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mi A
                      %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma, x:A \vdash \mathrm{refl}_A(x) : x =_A x}
          %p Elimination rule for identity types:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mi A
                      %mi y
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi t
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} refl
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mi A
                      %mi y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi t
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ind
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mo =
                            %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi t
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma, x:A, y:A, p:x =_A y \vdash C(x, y, p) \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma, x:A, t:C(x, x, \mathrm{refl}_A(x), y:A, p:x =_A y, \Delta(x, t, y, p) \vdash \mathrm{ind}_{=_A}(x, t, y, p):C(x, y, p)}
          %p Computation rules for identity types:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
