          %h2#categorical_semantics  Categorical semantics
          %p
            The fragment of propositional type theory consisting of only
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+types"} identity types
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product+types"} dependent product types
            can be interpreted in any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+category"} path category
            with weak homotopy
            = succeed "-types." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
          %h2#open_problems Open problems
          %p
            There are plenty of questions which are currently unresolved in propositional type theory.
            %a{:href => "#BB21"} Van den Berg and den Besten
            listed the following problems:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Does
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence"} univalence
                imply
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+extensionality"} function extensionality
                for types in the universe in
                = succeed "?" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+type+theory"} propositional type theory
            %li
              %p
                Is (the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
                based upon)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin-L%C3%B6f+type+theory"} Martin-Löf type theory
                conservative over (the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
                based upon)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+type+theory"} propositional
                Martin-Löf type theory?
            %li
              %p
                How much of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HoTT+book"} HoTT book
                could be done in
                = succeed "?" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+type+theory"} propositional type theory
            %li
              %p
                Does
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+type+theory"} propositional type theory
                have
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+canonicity"} homotopy canonicity
                and
                = succeed "?" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normalization"} normalization
          %p Other problems include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                What is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
                based upon
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+type+theory"} propositional type theory
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+inductive+types"} higher inductive types
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weakly+Tarski"} weakly Tarski
                = succeed "?" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalent+universes"} univalent universes
            %li
              %p
                Is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+function+extensionality"} weak function extensionality
                equivalent to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+extensionality"} function extensionality
                in
                = succeed "?" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+type+theory"} propositional type theory
            %li
              %p
                Does
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+extensionality"} product extensionality
                hold in
                = succeed "?" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+type+theory"} propositional type theory
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                and elements
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ×
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:A \times B
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
