                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{idtoprojectionids}:(a =_{A \times B} b) \to (\pi_1(a) \simeq \pi_1(b)) \times (\pi_2(a) \simeq \pi_2(b))
                an
                = succeed "?" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+types"} equivalence of types
            %li
              %p
                Is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+extensionality"} function extensionality
                still provable in propositional
                = succeed "?" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cubical+type+theory"} cubical type theory
          %p
            See also
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+problems+in+homotopy+type+theory"} open problems in homotopy type theory
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/judgmental+equality"}> judgmental equality
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+type"} identity type
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"}> dependent type theory
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin-L%C3%B6f+type+theory"} Martin-Löf type theory
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
          %h2#references  References
          %ul
            %li#Winterhalter20
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Th%C3%A9o+Winterhalter"}> Théo Winterhalter
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Formalisation and Meta-Theory of Type Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://github.com/TheoWinterhalter/phd-thesis/releases/download/v1.2.1/TheoWinterhalter-PhD-v1.2.1.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://github.com/TheoWinterhalter/phd-thesis"} github
            %li#Spadetto23
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matteo+Spadetto"}> Matteo Spadetto
                ,
                %em Relating homotopy equivalences to conservativity in dependendent type theories with propositional computation
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.05623"}> arXiv:2303.05623
                )
          %p On quadratic type checking in propositional type theory:
          %ul
            %li#BB21
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Benno+van+den+Berg"}> Benno van den Berg
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martijn+den+Besten"} Martijn den Besten
              %em Quadratic type checking for objective type theory
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2102.00905"}> arXiv:2102.00905
              )
          %p
            Talks at
            = succeed "," do
              %em Strength of Weak Type Theory
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/DutchCATS"} DutchCATS
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dani%C3%ABl+Otten"}> Daniël Otten
                ,
                %em Models for Propositional Type Theory
                (11 May 2023) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://dutchcats.github.io/Weak_type_theories/slides_otten.pdf"}> slides pdf
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Th%C3%A9o+Winterhalter"}> Théo Winterhalter
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A conservative and constructive translation from extensional type theory to weak type theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://dutchcats.github.io/Weak_type_theories/slides_winterhalter.pdf"} slides
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sam+Speight"}> Sam Speight
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Higher-Dimensional Realizability for Intensional Type Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://dutchcats.github.io/Weak_type_theories/slides_speight.pdf"} slides
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matteo+Spadetto"}> Matteo Spadetto
                ,
                %em Weak type theories: a conservativity result for homotopy elementary types
                (12 May 2023) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://dutchcats.github.io/Weak_type_theories/slides_spadetto.pdf"}> slides pdf
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Benno+van+den+Berg"}> Benno van den Berg
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Towards homotopy canonicity for propositional type theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://dutchcats.github.io/Weak_type_theories/slides_van_den_berg.pdf"} slides
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rafa%C3%ABl+Bocquet"}> Rafaël Bocquet
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Towards coherence theorems for equational extensions of type theories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://dutchcats.github.io/Weak_type_theories/slides_bocquet.pdf"} slides
          %p Talk at the Workshop on Homotopy Type Theory / Univalent Foundations 2024:
          %ul
            %li#Otten24
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dani%C3%ABl+Otten"}> Daniël Otten
              ,
              %em Models for Axiomatic Type Theory
              (
              %a{:href => "https://hott-uf.github.io/2024/slides/Otten.pdf"}> slides
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OT2fQ5iwRU"} video
          %p Talk at the WG6 meeting at Geneva in 2025:
          %ul
            %li#Spadetto25
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matteo+Spadetto"}> Matteo Spadetto
              , A 2-categorical approach to the sematics of axiomatic dependent type theory (
              %a{:href => "https://europroofnet.github.io/_pages/WG6/Genova/talks/spadetto.pdf"}> slides
              )
          %p
            Project to convert
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensional+type+theory"} extensional type theory
            to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+type+theory"} weak type theory
          %ul
            %li
              Github,
              %a{:href => "https://github.com/TheoWinterhalter/ett-to-wtt"} ett-to-wtt
          %p Additional general dependent type theory references used for the formalizations of propositional type theory in this article:
          %ul
            %li#UFP13
              %p
                %em> Homotopy Type Theory: Univalent Foundations of Mathematics
                , The
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Univalent+Foundations+Project"} Univalent Foundations Project
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://homotopytypetheory.org/book/"} web
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://hottheory.files.wordpress.com/2013/03/hott-online-323-g28e4374.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Rijke22
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Egbert+Rijke"}> Egbert Rijke
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Homotopy+Type+Theory"} Introduction to Homotopy Type Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.11082"} arXiv:2212.11082
            %li#CTZulip
              %p
                %em> Dependent Type Theory vs Polymorphic Type Theory
